    "message": "Add Vale prose gate and Diataxis docs tree\n\nLayer Google, write-good, and tbhb/vale-ai-tells v1.28.0 under a custom SSX360\nstyle with seven rules: banned marketing vocabulary, the em-dash ban, the\nnegative-parallelism tic, brand register on developer surfaces, verbose-term\nsubstitution, certification overclaims, and a whole-file compliance-hedge check\nwritten as a Tengo script because Vale's conditional extension compares literal\ncaptures and cannot express it.\n\nWire the gate into pre-commit (sync, prose, and commit-msg hooks) and into\nGitHub Actions via vale-cli/vale-action with fail_on_error, which reviewdog\nneeds to stop exiting 0 on reported errors.\n\nRestructure docs under Diataxis with MkDocs Material and mkdocstrings. Legacy\nflat docs stay authoritative and are excluded from the strict build until\nmigrated. mkdocs build --strict passes.\n\nPin remaining install examples to 0.6.1, matching pyproject.toml and the PyPI\nJSON API. Trim the README to four resolving badges, drop the tagline from the\ndeveloper surface, clear 25 em-dashes, and document how to verify the release\nagainst its PEP 740 attestation.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n",
